[Mods\Loading: music requests bigger blocks]
author=Namek025
description=CRI audio streams (music) request data when under 1/4 of the buffer is left, instead of as soon as 24 KB are consumed: fewer trips of the reader between music and data.
// func_0026A330 0x26A578: lw a0,0x1C(s3) (threshold) -> srl a0,v1,2 (buffer / 4). Also applies to streams already playing
patch=1,EE,0026A578,word,00032082

[Mods\Loading: music buffer x4]
author=Namek025
description=Each CRI audio handle's stream buffer is 4 times larger (BGM: ~160 KB -> ~640 KB, ~11 s of music): music barely reads from disc during a load. Together with "music requests bigger blocks": stage transition ~16.5 s -> ~9 s. Only affects handles created after the patch is applied (restart the game).
// igAdxAudio init (func_00331FB0): stream bytes = (_iMaxStreams + 1) * (freq/1000 * ch * 25000 / 44).
// 0x332030 sra a0,a0,3 (/44) -> sra a0,a0,1 (/11): x4. With sra a0,a0,0 (00042003) it would be x8.
patch=1,EE,00332030,word,00042043

[Mods\Loading: 512 KB read requests (experimental)]
author=Namek025
description=igAdxFile requests 512 KB from CRI instead of 128 KB. Try it together with "music requests bigger blocks".
// The 8 reads of igAdxFile._iBufferSize (+0x40) in func_00333860 (reserve) and func_00333D90 (read): lw rX,0x40(..) -> lui rX,0x8
patch=1,EE,00333898,word,3C040008
patch=1,EE,00333E9C,word,3C030008
patch=1,EE,00333F54,word,3C020008
patch=1,EE,00333F90,word,3C020008
patch=1,EE,00333FCC,word,3C040008
patch=1,EE,00334008,word,3C030008
patch=1,EE,003340C8,word,3C020008
patch=1,EE,0033410C,word,3C020008

